THIRD-PARTY DATA ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

This file records attribution for bundled data that carries an attribution
requirement. It exists because `data/DATA_SOURCES.md` was amended on 2026-08-09
to permit CC-BY licensed data alongside CC0 and public domain data, and CC-BY
requires that credit travel with the work.

Share-alike and non-commercial terms remain refused. See `data/DATA_SOURCES.md`
for the full policy and for the complete list of every source the project
touches, including the ones it deliberately refuses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CC-BY SOURCES CURRENTLY BUNDLED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None.

The policy permitting them is approved and no such file has been added yet. When
the first one lands, it is listed here with its title, author, licence version
and a link to the licence text, and `provenance.SOURCES` is updated in the same
change so `licence_audit()` can verify the claim.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CC0 AND PUBLIC DOMAIN SOURCES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These carry no attribution requirement and are credited here as a courtesy
rather than an obligation. `data/DATA_SOURCES.md` is the authoritative record.

  CPIC                Clinical Pharmacogenetics Implementation Consortium
                      CC0-1.0

  ClinVar             National Center for Biotechnology Information, NIH
                      US Government work, public domain

  gnomAD              Genome Aggregation Database, Broad Institute
                      CC0-1.0

  dbSNP               National Center for Biotechnology Information, NIH
                      US Government work, public domain

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TOOLS INVOKED AS SUBPROCESSES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DNAInsight can invoke external programs that the user installs themselves, into
their own home directory, outside this repository tree. None of them is
imported, linked, vendored or redistributed here, and the subprocess boundary is
the licence boundary. Their licences are their own and are recorded in
`backend/external.py` alongside each registry entry.
